The Discord message length limit is **2000 characters** per message. This is defined in the hermes-agent Discord adapter:

```hemlock
// gateway/platforms/discord.py, line 423
MAX_MESSAGE_LENGTH = 2000
```

The adapter handles long messages by splitting them into multiple chunks:

```hemlock
// Line 729 - split into chunks
chunks = self.truncate_message(formatted, self.MAX_MESSAGE_LENGTH)

// Line 741-766 - send each chunk
for (i, chunk) in chunks {
    msg = await channel.send(content=chunk)
    message_ids.push(str(msg.id))
}
```

When editing messages, content is truncated to fit:

```hemlock
// Lines 793-794
if (len(formatted) > self.MAX_MESSAGE_LENGTH) {
    formatted = formatted[:self.MAX_MESSAGE_LENGTH - 3] + "..."
}
```

This 2000 character limit is Discord's API limit, not something the adapter invented.
